          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Oleg Drokin",
          "email": "green@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-10-30 19:25:56.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Oleg Drokin",
          "email": "green@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-10-31 23:07:02.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "subject": "LU-20984 socklnd: check hello source PID before using it",
        "message": "LU-20984 socklnd: check hello source PID before using it\n\nksocknal_recv_hello() takes the peer's process id from the\nreceived HELLO and ksocknal_create_conn() uses it to create the\npeer.  The source NID is already checked for LNET_NID_ANY, but the\nsource PID is not checked at all.  A kernel LNet peer always uses\nLNET_PID_LUSTRE, and an outgoing connection already requires the\npeer to reply with the PID it was expected to have.\n\nReject a HELLO from a kernel peer whose source PID is not\nLNET_PID_LUSTRE with -EPROTO.  Userspace peers, whose PID is\nderived from their port, are not affected.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I235c2dcbf994dcb454b76feb0c076c4e1d48623c\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
